But if level beyond array, use last + (level - len)*80. Save `insights` cumulative. At level up subtract need. If user has huge insights from save? clamp. Implementation:
```
_insightNeed(){return this.level<=INSIGHT_STEPS.length ? INSIGHT_STEPS[this.level-1] : INSIGHT_STEPS[INSIGHT_STEPS.length-1]+(this.level-INSIGHT_STEPS.length)*70;}
_gainInsight(n){
 this.insights += n;
 let ups=0;
 while(this.insights >= this._insightNeed() && this.level < 30 && guard<20){
   this.insights -= this._insightNeed();
   this.level++;
   ups++;
 }
 if(ups) this.onLevelUp?.(this.level, this._levelTitle(this.level));
}
```
At level 1 need 12 insight. Player dream gives 1.2, teach +2.5; so reach level 2 after ~10 dreams. Fine.
